sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Coscinodiscus wailesii Turing wavelength at 4.3 mm (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — MorphoEval overall 80.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 implements spatial Schnakenberg kinetics and reports k_c = argmax sigma_+(k), calibrated so the nominal wavelength is 4.3 mm at age 0 Ma. The early-time power spectrum tracks lambda_sigma with Pearson r = 0.9899 and RMSE = 1.453 length units. The determinant-minimizer proxy anti-correlates (r = -0.919) and is rejected. Equal diffusivities decay (amplitude ratio 0.038). The upper-left SEM panel yields 718 areolae at pitch 10.15 px. The animated GIF is 12 frames at 640×480 and scores cv_sim_similarity 84.8 against the vendored plate. Overall 80.8/100 (faithfulness 78.0, reproducibility 87.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 594009 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 249a0ac9549fd79e067741c1b3146ab5d9dc3fc7ea9ad62b976399680541937a (sha256 249a0ac9549fd79e067741c1b3146ab5d9dc3fc7ea9ad62b976399680541937a), spec_fingerprint 7caaeeacf26efa87e18b214d7dcc8b05a2350b3e3c52eadcca8cd98bd3b11f89. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7caaeeacf26efa87e18b214d7dcc8b05a2350b3e3c52eadcca8cd98bd3b11f89; artifact_sha256: 249a0ac9549fd79e067741c1b3146ab5d9dc3fc7ea9ad62b976399680541937a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0/coscinodiscus_wailesii_specimen.jpg=cf556dab9e116068..., datasets/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=e1fca8ca30c9782c..., datasets/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=c6bf02023a4c27e5...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous reaction-diffusion equilibrium can select a stationary wavelength. | Schnakenberg 1979: trimolecular kinetics. The paper is well-mixed; the spatial PDE is a transfer. | Schmid and Volcani 1983: C. wailesii valve formation is centrifugal and proximal-to-distal, with distal cribra. | Edwards et al. 2001: the species persisted in the north-east Atlantic from 1977 through 1995.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian, sigma_+(q), and k_c = sqrt(argmax sigma_+). | Calibration of nominal lambda_sigma to 4.3 mm (0.004316 m). | Periodic spot integration, D_v sweep, equal-diffusivity ablation, and SEM pore segmentation.; transfer_boundary: 4.3 mm is the Delphi detail-scale wavelength for this slot, not a measured valve diameter. | The cohort form class is realized as areolar spots.; does_not_claim: That one frustule is 4.3 mm across. | That q_det is the selected wavenumber. | That SEM scale bars have been read as nanometres. | That a predecessor or successor chronospecies exists in this 1/1 series.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Expose a --dv/--seed probe so inhibitor diffusivity is a command-line regime, and print lambda_sigma against lambda_growth at that point.",
            "remediation needed: Headline the goodness of fit on the two-time Fourier growth-rate wavelength (empirical_growth_wavelength) and report its RMSE beside the 1.453 length-unit power-spectrum residual.",
            "remediation needed: Measure the disc-clamped valve interior standard deviation against the ablation amplitude so the margin boundary condition is a number, not only a panel." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.808"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (pass 1 assessment)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

